{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00Y3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$u^p$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-adjoint-point-push-stalk}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:974d0983b481fe8e2aafa2eada0941689ac04adff63c59cd60772198af2a0b46", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fd0cc3d9a956f122c2ce84d15c1442c2cdcf9e73501fcc838e53715349f01834", "source_text": "For any functor <MATH_0001>.\nThe functor <MATH_0002> is a right adjoint to the stalk functor\non presheaves.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:89f8fd1e8a2799bd12b5aff411b403a7b8914a2bf7826f941121b46618ca5516", "unit_id": "tag:00Y7:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00Y3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$E$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to u^pE$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\text{Map}(u(U), E)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\times u(U) \\to E$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}_p$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}_p \\to E$", "MATH_0009": "$(U, x, \\sigma)$", "MATH_0010": "$E$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\times u(U) \\to E$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-stalk}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2cb799a231fae1b004d0143376967aa7f8bbf99c45a4129822054feabba9a633", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:83eceb95603b60e126f5ee4aa4f058f14dae3e37adbb4e831dae6ea6a9dbff36", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a presheaf on <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a set. A morphism <MATH_0004>\nis given by a compatible system of maps\n<MATH_0005>, i.e.,\na compatible system of maps <MATH_0006>.\nAnd by definition of <MATH_0007> a map <MATH_0008>\nis given by a rule associating with each triple <MATH_0009>\nan element in <MATH_0010> such that equivalent triples map to the same element, see\ndiscussion surrounding\nEquation (<REF_0001>).\nThis also means a compatible system of maps <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:731b3541b87775eb1709cf55e80eb09e47079e0ab9e56108cbb2b6718d4c6346", "unit_id": "tag:00Y7:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00Y3", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{section-continuous-functors}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:61e0c4ca37a80577feede270922ee8cb7c47e26886eb8365b4f99a0888d3e64e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn analogy with Section <REF_0001>\nwe have the following lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d9861537d91c794e489df8234c5d44e6487585960ec6e914776663ac893fff8", "unit_id": "tag:00Y3:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00Y3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$p = u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\coprod u(U_i) \\to u(U)$", "MATH_0006": "$u(U_i \\times_U U_j) \\to u(U_i) \\times_{u(U)} u(U_j)$", "MATH_0007": "$u^pE$", "MATH_0008": "$E$", "MATH_0009": "$u^sE$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0011": "$u^s: \\textit{Sets} \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{F}_p = \\mathcal{F}^\\#_p$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0005": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\item", "STRUCT_0009": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-point-pushforward-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b2b248c51447dd0dd927f8c0997802fed7a618fad274027236530be3de6d331d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9070622675d82399f085499bc79724f5f4678f8212290da3da420f57bb5a88c5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a functor. Suppose that for every covering <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004>\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> the map <MATH_0005> is surjective, and\n<STRUCT_0003> the maps\n<MATH_0006> are surjective.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen we have\n<STRUCT_0005>\n<STRUCT_0006> the presheaf <MATH_0007> is a sheaf for all sets <MATH_0008>, denote it <MATH_0009>,\n<STRUCT_0007> the stalk functor <MATH_0010>\nand the functor <MATH_0011> are\nadjoint, and\n<STRUCT_0008> we have <MATH_0012>\nfor every presheaf of sets <MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0009>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dcf846ccc8e34f7e3c327bb64cc2a201c03c33ba9250953bf6662b37faaeb741", "unit_id": "tag:00Y8:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00Y3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u^pE$", "MATH_0002": "$u^p$", "MATH_0003": "$E$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\text{Map}(\\mathcal{F}_p, E) =\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(\\mathcal{F}, u^pE) =\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(\\mathcal{F}^\\#, u^sE) =\n\\text{Map}(\\mathcal{F}^\\#_p, E)\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-adjoint-point-push-stalk}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a0922a4fec443a3a47b324ee1f2a5dd1bf847c65a4fd58d837a7b4da991516cc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6129431eb19417e12d42d062ae4b0166b83ba6345775736ec74b676ee9cfd31a", "source_text": "The first assertion is immediate from the definition of a sheaf, assumptions\n(1) and (2), and the definition of <MATH_0001>. The second is a restatement of the\nadjointness of <MATH_0002> and the stalk functor\n(Lemma <REF_0001>) restricted to sheaves.\nThe third assertion follows as, for any set <MATH_0003>, we have\n<MATH_0004>\nby the adjointness property of sheafification.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d67d8a472b49a27779d53485ea02f1d8c8e2352c88bc8398a5cd7911f5e5d2b", "unit_id": "tag:00Y8:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00Y3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p = u$", "MATH_0002": "$u^sE$", "MATH_0003": "$E$", "MATH_0004": "$p$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-point-pushforward-sheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:30da1da739b6fefd12eef55b14a33af29a0b19975e7db248123c65991f50672b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5260925da0067e4f1ee6519b98907a7c17f8c7211254ffadcc3c915ab1dba527", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn particular Lemma <REF_0001>\nholds when <MATH_0001> is a point. In this case we think of the\nsheaf <MATH_0002> as the ``skyscraper'' sheaf with value <MATH_0003> at <MATH_0004>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3f6f0f93ee6900d0e7a492e42bc6fe76bc1172e11af5973680ace4f609af759d", "unit_id": "tag:00Y3:prose-0005"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00Y3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$u$", "MATH_0004": "$E$", "MATH_0005": "$p_*E = u^sE$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-point-pushforward-sheaf}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-pushforward-point}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:92864567235e3fc691577363fa0e5b69dd90d00a1937c70f9760177da7b58b7a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b52f14ce80ef35446111ec9ca3665e0ec96137c6e8de83fdf8e98ca4e60812df", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a point of the site <MATH_0002> given by the functor <MATH_0003>.\nFor a set <MATH_0004> we define <MATH_0005> the sheaf\ndescribed in Lemma <REF_0001> above.\nWe sometimes call this a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>skyscraper sheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0c173f22674366064d7a49ad98587128ddd3068626f4c98e97e53bfadcd438c0", "unit_id": "tag:00Y9:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00Y3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(\\mathcal{F}, p_*E)\n=\n\\text{Map}(\\mathcal{F}_p, E)\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$p^{-1}\\mathcal{F} = \\mathcal{F}_p$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e98656ba9ef098273680cb0ef01e542129a8f26e09753ead704158d8ae5cc32b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8f46b1de0cd60756053394cc8e945e7a494717dd3d0f85367fdbab7faa1c87ea", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn particular we have the following adjointness property\nof skyscraper sheaves and stalks:\n<MATH_0001>\nThis motivates the notation <MATH_0002>\nwhich we will sometimes use.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:db6ec138218a50716926eb49874c0f5b7138d4bb1893134ec2bc9956ae6c4145", "unit_id": "tag:00Y3:prose-0006"}
